---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Samedos GmbH"
  description="Privacy policy of Samedos GmbH in accordance with GDPR."
  lang="en"
  alternateHref="/datenschutz"
>
  <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6 py-24 space-y-12 [&_h2]:text-[1.4rem] [&_h2]:mb-4 [&_a]:text-mint [&_a:hover]:underline [&_strong]:text-navy">

    <div>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-muted mt-4">
        This privacy policy explains which personal data is processed when you visit our website
        and on what legal basis. A full legal privacy policy will be added in due course; for any
        questions please contact us at <a href="mailto:info@samedos.de">info@samedos.de</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section>
      <h2>Website Hosting</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-muted leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          Our website is hosted by <strong>Vercel Inc.</strong>, 440 N Barranca Avenue #4133,
          Covina, CA 91723, USA. Vercel operates servers in the European Union for our website.
        </p>
        <p>
          When you visit our site, technical data (IP address, browser type, requested URL,
          date/time) is automatically transmitted to Vercel and briefly stored in server logs.
          This is technically required to deliver the website.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Legal basis:</strong> Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (legitimate interest in error-free,
          secure operation). The data transfer to the US is based on the Standard Contractual
          Clauses under Art. 46 GDPR and our data processing agreement with Vercel.
        </p>
        <p>
          More information:
          <a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Content Management (CMS)</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-muted leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          Our website content is managed via <strong>Sanity AS</strong>, Strandgaten 6, 5013
          Bergen, Norway.
        </p>
        <p>
          Sanity stores and delivers website content (texts, images, job postings). No personal
          data of website visitors is collected.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Legal basis:</strong> Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR. A data processing agreement is in
          place.
        </p>
        <p>
          More information:
          <a href="https://www.sanity.io/legal/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">sanity.io/legal/privacy</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Contact Form &amp; Email Delivery</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-muted leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          When you use our contact form, the data you provide (name, email, optional phone,
          company name, message) is processed to handle your enquiry. Technical email delivery
          is handled by <strong>Resend, Inc.</strong>, 2261 Market Street #4382, San Francisco,
          CA 94114, USA.
        </p>
        <p>
          Resend forwards messages to our practice email and sends you an automated confirmation.
          Data transfer to the US is based on the Standard Contractual Clauses under Art. 46
          GDPR.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Legal basis:</strong> Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR (request handling) and Art. 6(1)(a)
          GDPR (your explicit consent by submitting the form).
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Retention:</strong> Enquiries are kept for as long as needed to handle them;
          Resend stores technical delivery logs for max. 30 days.
        </p>
        <p>
          More information:
          <a href="https://resend.com/legal/privacy-policy" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">resend.com/legal/privacy-policy</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Google Maps (Click-to-Load)</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-muted leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          On our contact page (<a href="/en/contact">/en/contact</a>) we show our location via a
          Google Maps view. Additionally, on <a href="/en/tour">/en/tour</a> we offer a virtual
          360° tour via Google Street View. Both services are provided by
          <strong>Google Ireland Limited</strong>, Gordon House, Barrow Street, Dublin 4,
          Ireland.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Important:</strong> The map / tour is loaded <strong>only after your explicit
          consent</strong>. Only when you click the "Show map" or "Start tour" button is a
          connection to Google servers established. At that point, technical data — including
          your IP address, browser and device information, and the page visited — is transmitted
          to Google. Google may forward this data to third countries, especially the United
          States.
        </p>
        <p>
          No data is transferred to Google before your consent.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Legal basis:</strong> Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR (consent). You may revoke your consent
          at any time by closing or leaving the page.
        </p>
        <p>
          More information:
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">policies.google.com/privacy</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Local Storage</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-muted leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          Our website uses your browser's local storage for a single technical function:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
          <li>
            <strong>Dismissed notifications:</strong> when you dismiss our "We are hiring"
            notice, we remember this for 7 days so the notice doesn't reappear.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          This data is stored only locally in your browser and is never transmitted to us or to
          third parties. You can delete this data at any time via your browser settings.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Legal basis:</strong> Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (legitimate interest in functionality
          and comfort).
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>
